🔖 Interactive tool for learning machine learning

A Python library has been released on GitHub that allows you to create your own datasets and use them for machine learning experiments.

Features:
🔵 Create 2D datasets directly in Jupyter;
🔵 Draw points and assign classes using the mouse;
🔵 Export data to pandas and Polars;
🔵 Pass samples to scikit-learn;
🔵 Experiment with classification and regression;
🔵 Update model training when data changes;
🔵 Works in Jupyter, VS Code, and Google Colab.

There is a demo version that you can try without installation.

⛓Link to GitHub
https://github.com/koaning/drawdata

